  "description": "CEGDEA crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C200 H272 Fe5 Gd4 N10 O40 1+,H1 O1 1-. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Fe3 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1A (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Fe2A (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Fe3A (Fe) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 25 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.089-5.079 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.58-169.87°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [FeIII5GdIII4(bis-C[4])2(μ4-O)2(μ3-O)2(μ3-NO3)2(dmf)8(H2O)6](OH). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies Fe(III), Gd(III).",
